# Install Inillucent

You are installing **Inillucent 1.0.29**, MIT licensed: an embedded SQL database with vector
and keyword search in one file. It installs `inillucent` (the command line, 30 verbs, `--output
json` on every one), `inillucent-shell` (shaped like `sqlite3`), `inillucent-mcp` (an MCP server,
28 tools), `inillucent-migrate` (SQLite, PostgreSQL or MySQL in, one verified database out), and the
C library with its header. Nothing is written outside the home directory and nothing needs
administrator rights.

## 1. Install, for this operating system

Check `uname -s` (`Darwin`, `Linux`) or for Windows, then follow one section.

### Windows

```powershell
irm https://inillucent.com/downloads/install.ps1 | iex
```

Unpacks into `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\inillucent` and adds its `bin` to the user PATH.

### Linux, x86-64 or ARM

```sh
curl -fsSL https://inillucent.com/downloads/install.sh | sh
```

The script reads `uname -m` and picks `x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu` or `aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu`
itself. It unpacks into `~/.local/share/inillucent` and links the four programs into
`~/.local/bin`. glibc 2.28 or newer.

### macOS

```sh
curl -fsSL https://inillucent.com/downloads/install.sh | sh
```

The same script as Linux. It picks the universal archive, which runs on Apple silicon and Intel,
and installs it the same way. There is also a signed installer package at
https://inillucent.com/downloads/inillucent-1.0.29.pkg.

## 2. PATH, if the script did not set it

Windows sets the user PATH itself, so open a new terminal; if the command is still not found, add
`%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\inillucent\bin`. On Linux and macOS add the bin directory, usually with
`export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"` in `~/.bashrc` or `~/.zshrc`.

## 3. Check it worked

```sh
inillucent --version
```

It must print `inillucent 1.0.29`. Not found means PATH, not the install: open a new terminal.

## 4. Make the first database

```sh
inillucent create app.rdb
inillucent --db app.rdb exec "CREATE TABLE note (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, body TEXT)"
inillucent --db app.rdb query "SELECT * FROM note"
```

Exit code 3 means "this engine has not built that", a different code from 1 on purpose: it is not a
syntax error, so do not start rewording the SQL.

## 5. Register the MCP server

Point `--root` at the directory the agent works in, so the server refuses every path resolving
outside it. `--readonly` refuses every statement that would change something; leave it off if the
agent should be able to write.

In **Claude Code** and in **Codex** the server command goes after a `--`:

```sh
claude mcp add inillucent -- inillucent-mcp --db app.rdb --root .
codex  mcp add inillucent -- inillucent-mcp --db app.rdb --root .
```

**Any other client**, in its own config:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "inillucent": {
      "command": "inillucent-mcp",
      "args": ["--db", "app.rdb", "--root", ".", "--readonly"]
    }
  }
}
```

Confirm it registered with `claude mcp list` or `codex mcp list`.

